{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>One to another.</b> Nation to nation — Egypt to Cush, and Cush to Put, and Put to Canaan." "<b>Come.</b> Prepare yourselves. Every הָבָה is a term of preparation — that they ready themselves and join together for a task, or for counsel, or for a burden. הָבָה — prepare; אפר\"לייר בלע\"ז." "<b>For bricks.</b> For there are no stones in Babylon, for it is a valley." "<b>And burn them for burning.</b> Thus they make the bricks called טוויל\"ש בל' — they burn them in a kiln." "<b>For mortar.</b> To plaster the wall."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French apareillier, 'to prepare/ready'", 3 "the la'az טוויל\"ש is Old French tuile, 'tile/brick'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:58:17.942575926Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}